            <ArticleTitle>[Laparoscopic cystectomy-urinary diversion with robotic assistance : which future ?]</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2094-2096</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Known for its significant morbidity, radical cystectomy must improve minimally invasively. Rapidly but sporadically initiated at the beginning of the robotic era 15 years ago, laparoscopic cystectomy-urinary diversion has slowly progressed technically. It is actually optimally standardized to be entirely performed intra-corporealy. Its technical difficulty remaining high, robotic cystectomy should remain in expert hands with a significant recruitement to remain performant.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
